From: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: fix the ring setup unwind loops

Every ring setup loop that unwinds after a failed allocation counts down
with an unsigned index and tests it against zero:

	u32 ring_idx;
	...
		while (--ring_idx >= 0)
			edma_cfg_rx_fill_ring_cleanup(&edma_ctx->rxfill_rings[ring_idx]);

The condition can never be false.  The loop cleans up the rings that
were set up, then decrements past zero to UINT_MAX and keeps going,
indexing gigabytes beyond the array and passing whatever it finds to a
cleanup function that dereferences it.  The Tx loops spell the same
non-terminating test as "while (i-- >= 0)".

This is reached whenever dma_alloc_coherent() fails while the rings are
being set up.  It is silent at build time: -Wtype-limits is a W=2
warning.

Count down with the loop variable itself, which stops the loops at the
first ring and leaves what they visit otherwise unchanged: the rings
that were set up, and not the one whose setup failed, which frees its
own partial state before returning.

Signed-off-by: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_rx.c
@@ -586,7 +586,7 @@ static int edma_cfg_rx_rings_setup(void)
 		if (ret) {
 			pr_err("Error in setting up %d rxfill ring. ret: %d",
 			       rxfill_ring->ring_id, ret);
-			while (--ring_idx >= 0)
+			while (ring_idx-- > 0)
 				edma_cfg_rx_fill_ring_cleanup(&edma_ctx->rxfill_rings[ring_idx]);
 
 			return -ENOMEM;
@@ -605,7 +605,7 @@ static int edma_cfg_rx_rings_setup(void)
 
 		if (queue_id > EDMA_CPU_PORT_QUEUE_MAX(EDMA_RX_QUEUE_START)) {
 			pr_err("Invalid queue_id: %d\n", queue_id);
-			while (--ring_idx >= 0)
+			while (ring_idx-- > 0)
 				edma_cfg_rx_desc_ring_cleanup(&edma_ctx->rx_rings[ring_idx]);
 
 			goto rxdesc_mem_alloc_fail;
@@ -624,7 +624,7 @@ static int edma_cfg_rx_rings_setup(void)
 		if (ret) {
 			pr_err("Error in setting up %d rxdesc ring. ret: %d",
 			       rxdesc_ring->ring_id, ret);
-			while (--ring_idx >= 0)
+			while (ring_idx-- > 0)
 				edma_cfg_rx_desc_ring_cleanup(&edma_ctx->rx_rings[ring_idx]);
 
 			goto rxdesc_mem_alloc_fail;
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_tx.c
@@ -400,7 +400,7 @@ static int edma_cfg_tx_rings_setup(void)
 		if (ret) {
 			pr_err("Error in setting up %d txdesc ring. ret: %d",
 			       txdesc_ring->id, ret);
-			while (i-- >= 0)
+			while (i-- > 0)
 				edma_cfg_tx_desc_ring_cleanup(&edma_ctx->tx_rings[i]);
 
 			return -ENOMEM;
@@ -420,7 +420,7 @@ static int edma_cfg_tx_rings_setup(void)
 		if (ret != 0) {
 			pr_err("Error in setting up %d Tx cmpl ring. ret: %d",
 			       txcmpl_ring->id, ret);
-			while (i-- >= 0)
+			while (i-- > 0)
 				edma_cfg_txcmpl_ring_cleanup(&edma_ctx->txcmpl_rings[i]);
 
 			goto txcmpl_mem_alloc_fail;
